1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} My uncle Leif Harry Berger was born at Berger, Degernes, Norway, to father Johan Albert Olsen Berger and mother Marie Johansdatter.  Leif’s mother Marie died when her children were relatively young. At one point, a
2 CONC round the 1930’s, Leif lived with his father, 3 brothers and 3 sisters on Bakkegata in Sannesund, Sarpsborg, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif moved to Degernes, Norway before 1940 and he worked for a while mining quarts and minerals with his brother Erling at the Thiis mines and various other mines in Degernes. Leif built his home at Sandbekk shortly after the 1940
2 CONC -1945 war ended and he lived there until he died in 1993.
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember Leif and Magna visited us on the week-end sometimes. The grown-ups would play Monopoly and Dominoes for hours on end as my brother and I would play outside with our cousins.   And our family would visit Leif and Magna a
2 CONC s well.  It was always fun to visit, we would get out the bicycles and start pedaling.  My father never owned a car, so it was the bicycle or bus that got us around, mostly the bicycle. Uncle Leif had a motorcycle, a 125 cc Tempo,
2 CONC  Villiers.  This was an amazing machine and we never got tired of looking at it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif would often come on his motorcycle to watch the Degernes soccer team whenever they had home-games on Saturdays. Leif also liked to go fishing at “fjella”, not far from Sandbekk and he sometimes vent there with my father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Egil Berger 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Notes by Egil Berger 2013'''
2 CONT
2 CONT My uncle Leif Harry Berger was born at Berger, Degernes, Norway, to father Johan Albert Olsen Berger and mother Marie Johansdatter.  Leif’s mother Marie died when her children were relatively young. At one point, around the 1930’s
2 CONC , Leif lived with his father, 3 brothers and 3 sisters on Bakkegata in Sannesund, Sarpsborg, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif moved back to Degernes, Norway before 1940 and he worked for a while mining quarts and minerals with his brother Erling at the Thiis mines and various other mines in Degernes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif built his home at Sandbekk shortly after the 1940-1945 war ended and he lived there until he died in 1993. I remember Leif and Magna visited us on the week-end sometimes. The grown-ups would play Monopoly and Dominoes for hou
2 CONC rs on end as my brother and I would play outside with our cousins.  
2 CONT
2 CONT And our family would visit Leif and Magna as well.  It was always fun to visit, we would get out the bicycles and start pedaling.  My father never owned a car, so it was the bicycle or bus that got us around, mostly the bicycle. U
2 CONC ncle Leif had a motorcycle, a 125 cc Tempo, Villiers.  This was an amazing machine and we never got tired of looking at it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif would often come on his motorcycle to watch the Degernes soccer team whenever they had home-games on Saturdays.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif also liked to go fishing at “fjella”, not far from Sandbekk and he sometimes vent there with my father.
